# .release-removals — deliberate deletions against the PUBLISHED tree.
#
# One path or path-prefix per line; `#` comments allowed. The `[6/6] public-regress`
# gate blocks any release that removes a file already on public `master` unless it is
# declared here. A deletion is not forbidden — it must be intended, and this file is
# the reviewed record that it was.
#
# A comment-only or blank file is NOT an allow-all; it declares nothing.

# ── [ADR-0031] — the rolling status log moved to `docs/STATUS.md` ──────────────
# `docs/status/STATUS.md` has been public since v0.8.0. It is not withdrawn: it moved
# one directory up to `docs/STATUS.md`, and its `[[doc]]` block in CANONICAL-DOCS.toml
# is repointed in the same commit as this line. Same file, same content, shorter path.
#
# Why move it. `docs/status/` is for DATED, episodic snapshots — handoffs, checkpoints,
# point-in-time notes — which are working memory and publish nothing. The single rolling
# log is the opposite: it is how this repo says out loud where it stands, and it is
# canonical. Two kinds of document in one directory, separated only by remembering which
# filename was the exception. After the move they separate by PATH, which is a property
# a tool can check instead of a convention a person has to recall.
#
# Unusually clean here: `docs/status/` held this one file and nothing else, so the move
# empties the directory rather than sorting it.
#
# Declared with the EXACT path, not the `docs/status` prefix. A bare directory entry
# would silently authorize removing anything ever published beneath it — a standing
# permission granted for a one-time move. This entry authorizes exactly the file that
# moved, and nothing else.
#
# Declared even though the gate may not ask for it. `public_regression_ok` runs
# `git diff --diff-filter=D` with rename detection on, so a pure move like this one is
# likely to resolve as a rename and pass silently. Declaring only what the gate happens
# to notice would make this file a record of the tool's blind spot rather than of our
# intent. Reversible: `git mv` it back and drop this line.
docs/status/STATUS.md
